WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.279 --> 00:00:05.250
Nobody should ever have to find out what a
human body smells like.

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:08.300
Especially as it's being eaten.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:13.660
Sally clasped both hands over her face, trying
desperately to block out the smell and to

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:16.189
trap in her nervous breathing.

00:00:16.189 --> 00:00:18.890
She couldn't bring herself to look.

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:23.430
Every bone in her body wanted to take off
running through the forest, back out onto

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:27.029
the interstate, to try and find some help.

00:00:27.029 --> 00:00:29.130
But there was nothing she could do.

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:32.649
She could never outrun that... thing.

00:00:32.649 --> 00:00:35.840
It was too fast, too savage.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:40.000
Even if she could convince someone on the
highway to pull over and help her, they would

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.480
just tell her she was going crazy.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:44.500
Maybe she was.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:49.970
Then the smell of her husband's body drifted
over to her on the wind as the crunching sound

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:53.309
of inhuman jaws filled the air.

00:00:53.309 --> 00:00:54.449
Panic set in.

00:00:54.449 --> 00:00:56.120
Then silence.

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:59.930
She couldn't hear anything, not even a whisper
in the trees.

00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:01.160
Had she done it?

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:02.680
Had she survived?

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:08.110
That's when a red sneaker stepped out from
behind the tree, and Sally stared into the

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:10.840
eyes of the blood-spattered hedgehog.

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:11.840
*

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:14.060
Now, Sally had never been a gamer growing
up.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:18.900
Sure, she played a little bit of Mario Kart
and had a few Nintendogs back in the day,

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:21.700
but the word "gamer," just wasn't for her.

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:26.360
However, love conquers all, and when she found
the man of her dreams, she decided that it

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:30.040
would be worth at least giving some of his
hobbies a go.

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:34.540
They started off nice and easy, playing a
bit of Stardew Valley, Minecraft, and maybe

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:37.020
some Overcooked here and there.

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:41.750
But before long, the pair of them were sitting
down every day after work, headsets on and

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:46.430
controllers in hand, ready to dive into the
latest adventure.

00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:50.680
Just recently, the couple had gotten into
retro games, going back and playing classics

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:53.530
like Battletoads and Streets of Rage.

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:55.649
The challenge was addictive.

00:01:55.649 --> 00:02:01.930
So when her husband John came home with a
copy of an unmarked NES game, Sally was intrigued

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:03.390
to say the least.

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:07.950
John explained to her that he had found it
listed on eBay under a very suspicious account.

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:13.099
He had gone to pick up the game after work
that day, expecting to be greeted by the smiling

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:14.510
face of the seller.

00:02:14.510 --> 00:02:19.030
Instead, he had found a blank gray cartridge
and a very brief manual wrapped together with

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:21.970
an elastic band on a street corner.

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:27.050
The seller had listed it for virtually nothing,
and based on the description, seemed very

00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:30.110
eager to get rid of the game for some reason.

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:34.849
So eager that he must not have wanted to stick
around to even hand it over.

00:02:34.849 --> 00:02:39.080
Sally, already bored with this backstory,
snatched the manual up and read the title

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:43.640
of the game: "Professor Gould's Terrifying
Horror Challenge.”

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:50.400
There was no artwork, no branding, no publisher,
no stickers—nothing to differentiate this

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:53.530
game from being just a blank cartridge.

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:58.530
As far as Sally knew, it could have even been
a virus, some kind of malware game designed

00:02:58.530 --> 00:02:59.880
to brick their NES.

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:04.280
But the words "horror" and "challenge" from
the title sold her.

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:08.910
She blew on the pins in the cartridge and
slotted it into place in the NES.

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:15.190
A black screen appeared with nothing on it
but two options: single player or two player.

00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:18.780
Sally uncoiled a second controller and handed
it to John with a grin.

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:20.080
"You ready?"

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:25.140
Sally hit two-player, and a new screen came
up: "Are the people holding the controllers

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:27.670
the people who want to play the game?

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:29.640
Yes or no."

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:30.640
Sally hit yes.

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:35.920
A shrill beep filled the room, high-pitched
and grating on their ears.

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:40.159
John immediately grabbed for the remote and
turned the volume down on the TV, but the

00:03:40.159 --> 00:03:42.189
beep just kept going.

00:03:42.189 --> 00:03:46.960
The screen was a bright red, filling the room
with an unnatural bloody light.

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:52.300
John tried to hit the off button on the remote,
but the TV stayed red, and the beeping sound

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:55.560
continued, filling their tiny apartment.

00:03:55.560 --> 00:04:00.680
Getting up and rushing over to the TV, John
tried to unplug it, but it was no use.

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:03.200
The beeping noise and the red screen persisted.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:09.239
He looked back at his wife in confusion, but
she was looking elsewhere entirely.

00:04:09.239 --> 00:04:15.920
There was a rat in the corner of the room,
with mottled fur, bloated flesh, and cracked

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:16.920
teeth.

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:20.690
It stared right into Sally's eyes, salivating.

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:24.580
Without a moment's hesitation, she leaped
up onto the couch and screamed.

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:30.600
But instead of running away, the rat slowly
crept forward, looking almost as if it was

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:31.600
smiling.

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:36.040
Then a second one appeared, crawling out from
behind the couch, followed by a third in the

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:39.610
doorway and a fourth beneath the TV.

00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:44.740
Dozens of rats filled the room, swarming in
from all directions, climbing over one another

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:50.889
in a desperate attempt to get into the tiny
apartment, to get to Sally and John.

00:04:50.889 --> 00:04:55.550
Sally clambered onto the couch with her laptop
and tried to kick away any of the rats clambering

00:04:55.550 --> 00:04:58.770
up onto the furniture, but it was no use.

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:04.000
For every rat she kicked away, another one
appeared, until soon they were climbing their

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:09.600
way up John's jeans, their sharp little claws
digging into his flesh.

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:14.650
The rats tore at Sally's clothes, climbing
over one another desperately, heading towards

00:05:14.650 --> 00:05:17.500
her mouth, trying to burrow their way in.

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:22.340
Hairy bodies filled her vision, and the stench
of disease made her gag.

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:27.970
Seizing an opportunity, a rat tried to clamber
through her open jaws; she felt its tiny paws

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:29.820
scrabbling at her tongue.

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:34.220
With tears filling her eyes, she took one
fleeting look at the man she loved and…

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:36.479
noticed something behind him.

00:05:36.479 --> 00:05:40.789
A giant yellow bottle with the words "rat
poison" stamped into the side was sitting

00:05:40.789 --> 00:05:43.170
precariously on top of their cabinet.

00:05:43.170 --> 00:05:47.880
Half stumbling, half swimming, Sally pushed
her way through the throng of rats filling

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:52.509
their apartment and desperately grabbed the
bottle from on top of the cabinet.

00:05:52.509 --> 00:05:57.110
Throwing the rats off her hands, she managed
to unscrew the lid, held the bottle high over

00:05:57.110 --> 00:06:02.690
her head, and poured the thick, stinking liquid
all over the swarm of rats threatening to

00:06:02.690 --> 00:06:03.860
engulf her.

00:06:03.860 --> 00:06:09.000
The chorus of death filled the room, whether
it was the sound of the rats dying or their

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:13.750
bodies being evaporated by the poison, she
couldn't tell.

00:06:13.750 --> 00:06:19.250
All she could do was push through to try and
find her husband and save him too.

00:06:19.250 --> 00:06:24.220
And miraculously, within just a few seconds,
all of the rats had disappeared.

00:06:24.220 --> 00:06:27.800
The room was empty, the same as it had always
been.

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:30.610
Even the big yellow bottle was gone from her
hand.

00:06:30.610 --> 00:06:36.940
All she could do was stare at John as he stared
back at her, as the words "Level 1 complete"

00:06:36.940 --> 00:06:39.080
appeared above their heads.

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:40.080
*

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:47.539
Welcome to SCP-1315, the most visceral, most
real, and most dangerous horror game you will

00:06:47.539 --> 00:06:50.509
ever have the misfortune of playing.

00:06:50.509 --> 00:06:55.190
It's not too late to back out at the menu
screen when you select how many players you

00:06:55.190 --> 00:06:58.860
want; it's not even too late at the confirmation
screen.

00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:02.080
But once you're in the game, there's no turning
back.

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:06.949
Either you beat the game, or you die trying.

00:07:06.949 --> 00:07:09.039
Beating this game is no easy feat.

00:07:09.039 --> 00:07:15.949
A copy of SCP-1315 has been in Foundation
containment since 1986, but in all of that

00:07:15.949 --> 00:07:19.949
time, only one D-Class personnel has managed
to make it to Level 33.

00:07:19.949 --> 00:07:25.780
It is not known how many levels there are,
but there is theoretically a final boss.

00:07:25.780 --> 00:07:30.259
The reason why no one has been able to beat
it thus far is that with each level, the difficulty

00:07:30.259 --> 00:07:32.479
of the game increases.

00:07:32.479 --> 00:07:37.940
Relatively minor challenges in the first few
levels give way to extremely difficult, life-threatening

00:07:37.940 --> 00:07:40.980
scenarios as the player progresses.

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:46.190
These levels broadly follow the same pattern
each time, but individual levels often contain

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:48.520
an element of randomness.

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:53.849
For example, Level 1 that Sally and John played
contained rats, but other tests have shown

00:07:53.849 --> 00:07:59.349
subjects being swarmed by insects and spiders,
often coinciding with established phobias

00:07:59.349 --> 00:08:02.699
that the subject has reported prior to the
experiment.

00:08:02.699 --> 00:08:05.840
Two hours later, John and Sally were running
low on ammo.

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:10.750
With both couches pushed against the door
to the lounge, they both hunkered down behind

00:08:10.750 --> 00:08:15.030
the TV, loading the remains of their shells
into the shotguns.

00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:19.789
From out in the hallway, they could hear the
heavy footsteps of more animals rushing towards

00:08:19.789 --> 00:08:20.789
them.

00:08:20.789 --> 00:08:24.720
When the pounding on their door had first
started, they assumed it had been their neighbor

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:29.789
coming up to complain about their screaming
and running around in the previous levels.

00:08:29.789 --> 00:08:33.800
John had been so deep in thought, trying to
work out what their cover story could be,

00:08:33.800 --> 00:08:38.050
that when he opened the door and saw an adult
grizzly bear standing on its hind legs in

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:42.260
front of him, it had taken him almost too
long to react.

00:08:42.260 --> 00:08:46.850
Sprinting back into the lounge, he found his
wife already loading rounds into the shotgun

00:08:46.850 --> 00:08:49.830
that had suddenly appeared on the floor in
front of her.

00:08:49.830 --> 00:08:54.920
With a grim expression on her face, she seemed
to have accepted their new reality—that

00:08:54.920 --> 00:08:58.570
this was a game they were going to have to
fight their way through.

00:08:58.570 --> 00:09:03.700
But with every bear that they shot as it tried
to push its way into their lounge, two more

00:09:03.700 --> 00:09:05.800
had appeared just minutes later.

00:09:05.800 --> 00:09:09.930
While they had been conservative with their
ammo, aiming for the heads and not taking

00:09:09.930 --> 00:09:14.079
any risks, the pair was starting to run dangerously
low.

00:09:14.079 --> 00:09:16.090
Was there an objective they were missing?

00:09:16.090 --> 00:09:19.790
Were they supposed to have done something
to progress through the level?

00:09:19.790 --> 00:09:24.029
Sally mashed a couple of buttons on the NES
controller, and then some text appeared on

00:09:24.029 --> 00:09:28.100
the red screen: Objective: Survive.

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:31.660
Four bears appeared in the doorway and pushed
hard against the couch.

00:09:31.660 --> 00:09:35.170
It slid out of the way, and they charged into
the room.

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:39.060
Sally and John desperately took down the first
two of them, but the dreaded click of the

00:09:39.060 --> 00:09:42.110
triggers told them that they had nothing left.

00:09:42.110 --> 00:09:45.860
Closing their eyes and bracing themselves
for the worst, the pounding of heavy paws

00:09:45.860 --> 00:09:48.140
on their vinyl floor suddenly stopped.

00:09:48.140 --> 00:09:49.920
The bears had disappeared.

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:51.890
Level 3 complete.

00:09:51.890 --> 00:09:54.700
"Well, whatever's next can't be worse than
that, surely."

00:09:54.700 --> 00:09:56.260
But it was.

00:09:56.260 --> 00:09:59.769
They managed to hold out in their apartment
until level 9.

00:09:59.769 --> 00:10:05.310
But then the windows behind their heads smashed
into a thousand shards as a black-booted SWAT

00:10:05.310 --> 00:10:07.290
team swung into the room.

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:12.079
With barely any time to react, Sally and John
pushed their way out of the apartments and

00:10:12.079 --> 00:10:14.380
braced themselves down to their car.

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:19.060
Slamming both doors closed, they took off,
racing towards the highway as the SWAT vehicles

00:10:19.060 --> 00:10:20.310
pursued them.

00:10:20.310 --> 00:10:23.269
Three hours later, the couple was running
low on gas.

00:10:23.269 --> 00:10:27.829
Swerving their way along the interstate, their
eyes on the mirrors constantly, the pair was

00:10:27.829 --> 00:10:31.320
pretty certain they'd managed to lose their
assailants.

00:10:31.320 --> 00:10:35.399
Slowing their car to the speed limit, they
gently weaved their way through the traffic

00:10:35.399 --> 00:10:37.610
towards the nearest gas station.

00:10:37.610 --> 00:10:41.910
Trying their best not to look suspicious,
the two of them went inside, keen to stock

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:43.450
up on supplies.

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:46.029
Who knew how long this game would go on for?

00:10:46.029 --> 00:10:49.320
They had already been active for hours and
were exhausted.

00:10:49.320 --> 00:10:53.870
With the SWAT team hopefully long behind them
now, the adrenaline rush was starting to wear

00:10:53.870 --> 00:10:57.210
off, and the reality of this situation was
starting to set in.

00:10:57.210 --> 00:11:01.240
Hopefully, there were just ten levels, and
they only had one to go.

00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:06.180
But with a sinking feeling in their chests,
each of them realized it was more likely to

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:07.889
be 100.

00:11:07.889 --> 00:11:10.980
Definitely time to stock up on some supplies.

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:16.089
They were barely halfway around the gas station
when the words "Level 9 complete" flashed

00:11:16.089 --> 00:11:17.959
in the sky above them.

00:11:17.959 --> 00:11:22.030
Both John and Sally froze where they were
and stared at each other over the aisles.

00:11:22.030 --> 00:11:27.709
A blue flash darted past them outside the
windows, then again going the other way.

00:11:27.709 --> 00:11:30.180
Sally ran over to the counter and banged on
the glass.

00:11:30.180 --> 00:11:31.870
"Lock the door, lock the door!"

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:34.660
But the teenager just looked at her in confusion.

00:11:34.660 --> 00:11:40.000
And now it was Sally's turn to look around
and see her husband staring in horror.

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:46.730
On the other side of the glass, standing between
two gas pumps, was Sonic.exe.

00:11:46.730 --> 00:11:52.170
With haunting red eyes, rows and rows of sharp
teeth, and blood dripping from his mouth,

00:11:52.170 --> 00:11:55.320
the hedgehog stared intently.

00:11:55.320 --> 00:11:59.100
Sally pointed out the window and turned to
the teenager, yelling, but the girl took a

00:11:59.100 --> 00:12:01.329
step back, looking scared of her.

00:12:01.329 --> 00:12:03.220
The girl couldn't see it.

00:12:03.220 --> 00:12:05.040
She couldn't see Sonic.

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:10.029
For all these challenges, all the things they'd
been fighting... was it just in her head?

00:12:10.029 --> 00:12:12.459
But there was no time to worry about that.

00:12:12.459 --> 00:12:15.459
Sally jumped the counter and ran towards the
door to the back of the shop, hearing the

00:12:15.459 --> 00:12:17.779
footsteps of her husband running after her.

00:12:17.779 --> 00:12:20.040
She kicked open the fire exit but froze immediately.

00:12:20.040 --> 00:12:24.570
Sonic.exe was standing there in front of her,
smiling.

00:12:24.570 --> 00:12:26.600
It was toying with them.

00:12:26.600 --> 00:12:29.220
They needed to run, to get out of here as
quickly as possible.

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:32.010
But how could they outrun Sonic?

00:12:32.010 --> 00:12:33.350
"Hey, Sonic!"

00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:34.680
John yelled from behind her.

00:12:34.680 --> 00:12:35.700
"You hungry?"

00:12:35.700 --> 00:12:40.140
He pushed Sally out of the way and threw a
handful of chili dogs out into the forest.

00:12:40.140 --> 00:12:45.230
Hearing "hungry," Sonic spun around and chased
after his favorite food as quickly as possible.

00:12:45.230 --> 00:12:50.500
That had only bought them a few moments of
time, but maybe that was all they'd get.

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:53.910
Sally and John ran back through the convenience
store and out the front.

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:57.769
They couldn’t run, but they could at least
try to hide.

00:12:57.769 --> 00:13:02.079
A semi-truck had to slam on the brakes as
the pair of them ran across the interstate.

00:13:02.079 --> 00:13:05.790
Without a choice of running anywhere else,
all they could do was dart into the woods

00:13:05.790 --> 00:13:09.850
on the other side and hope that Sonic had
a bad sense of smell.

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:15.020
But as they ran through the woods, they could
hear an ominous voice echoing behind them.

00:13:15.020 --> 00:13:17.980
"Got to go fast, got to go faster than that."

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:21.829
Sally found a tree and dived into cover just
at the right moment.

00:13:21.829 --> 00:13:23.950
Her husband wasn't so lucky.

00:13:23.950 --> 00:13:29.250
There was a flash of blue and a horrible crunching
sound before his body hit the ground.

00:13:29.250 --> 00:13:35.100
Sonic.exe was on top of him in a heartbeat,
rows of sharp teeth gnashing.

00:13:35.100 --> 00:13:40.220
Sally clasped both hands over her face, trying
desperately to block out the smell and trap

00:13:40.220 --> 00:13:41.660
her nervous breathing.

00:13:41.660 --> 00:13:43.620
She couldn't bring herself to look.

00:13:43.620 --> 00:13:48.149
Every bone in her body wanted to take off
running through the forest, out onto the road

00:13:48.149 --> 00:13:50.310
to try and find some help.

00:13:50.310 --> 00:13:52.410
But there was nothing she could do.

00:13:52.410 --> 00:13:55.430
She could never outrun that... thing.

00:13:55.430 --> 00:13:58.399
It was too fast, too savage.

00:13:58.399 --> 00:14:02.370
Even if she could convince someone on the
highway to pull over and help her, they would

00:14:02.370 --> 00:14:05.079
just tell her she was going crazy.

00:14:05.079 --> 00:14:06.079
Maybe she was.

00:14:06.079 --> 00:14:11.150
Then the smell of her husband's body drifted
over to her on the wind as the crunching sound

00:14:11.150 --> 00:14:14.220
of inhuman jaws filled her ears.

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:15.740
New tears flowed.

00:14:15.740 --> 00:14:17.790
Then silence.

00:14:17.790 --> 00:14:21.529
She couldn't hear anything, not even a whisper
in the trees.

00:14:21.529 --> 00:14:22.529
Had she done it?

00:14:22.529 --> 00:14:23.529
Had she survived?

00:14:23.529 --> 00:14:28.649
Then a red sneaker stepped out from behind
the tree, and Sally stared into the eyes of

00:14:28.649 --> 00:14:32.070
the blood-spattered, deranged Hedgehog.

00:14:32.070 --> 00:14:34.070
Sally blinked, and it was gone.

00:14:34.070 --> 00:14:36.110
Level 10 complete.

00:14:36.110 --> 00:14:38.600
The open forest stretched out in front of
her.

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:43.350
Without a moment to catch her breath, Sally
